<li>Check how much time you can give to regular preparation.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Assess your current English honestly</h2>
<p>A test format cannot replace language ability. Before focusing heavily on templates or shortcuts, identify the areas that need development. You may need stronger grammar and vocabulary, clearer organization in writing, more accurate reading, or greater confidence producing spoken English under time limits.</p>
<p>A useful preparation plan combines familiarity with the exam format and continued language practice. Ask how class activities address the learning areas published in the course outline and how students receive feedback during the current batch.</p>

<h2>Compare the preparation courses</h2>
<p>Open the current IELTS and PTE course pages and compare their learning focus, duration, fee and listed faculty information. Then ask practical questions:</p>
<ul>
<li>What starting level will help me participate effectively?</li>
<li>How are speaking and writing practice handled?</li>
